{
 "_doc": "What each Wax Hall reenactor does over the scene's loop. Hand-authored from parts/waxscenes.js: the web scenes pose joint angles frame by frame, Unreal plays retargeted motion capture instead, so each figure gets a list of beats. A beat is {t: seconds into the loop, a: action id, y: degrees added to the figure's yaw while it plays, r: play rate, b: crossfade seconds, l: centimetres to lift the figure (seated clips sit at the clip's own seat height)}. The action id names an AnimSequence at /Game/WTA/Characters/Common/Anims/Mocap/AS_WTA_<id>, retargeted from Mixamo by Content/Python/wta_mocap. The last beat runs to the end of the loop and crossfades back into the first, so the loop is seamless. Props ride the figures: each key is {t, f: figure (empty = stands still in the stage's own frame), s: socket (head/hand_l/hand_r/chest), o: offset cm, r: rotation deg, b: seconds to travel from the previous key}. A key in a hand needs no offset: the stage sets the prop's own frame in the palm (+X along the fingers, +Y out of the palm) and closes that hand's fingers round it (World/WTAWaxStageActor.cpp WaxGrip); o and r there are extras on top of that. A prop's web is the index of the S.carry call that made it in parts/waxscenes.js: the web export (unreal/Pipeline/web/export_campus.py) writes that object as the mesh prop__<scene>_<web> of Props.glb, in its own frame, and the stage rides it instead of a block. Carries the acting data does not ride (a laptop on a desk, a case lid) still come across: build_data.py adds them from out/campus/props_rest.json, standing where the web left them. A scene's place {var: {at, ry}} stands that figure somewhere other than the web put it (web metres in the stage group's frame, +z toward the walkway). Whoever holds or wears a prop keeps still while they have it (a prop is never held perfectly, so a hand or head that moves makes it look glitchy): their beats in that time are their pose's still clip (tablet, phone, carry, idle, sit_idle, kneel), and they do not turn.",
